From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: a taskbar on every display

David 2026-11-12: "many monitors, more than two even ... which gets the task bar, or if all
of them get the task bar". As on Windows: the main taskbar is on the main display, and with
"Show taskbar on all displays" (Explorer\Advanced MMTaskbarEnabled, on by default) each other
display has a bar of its own (Shell_SecondaryTrayWnd) on the same edge, with Start (it opens
on that display), the windows' buttons and the clock, and reserving that display's work area.
"Show taskbar buttons on" (MMTaskbarMode): all taskbars; the main taskbar and the one where
the window is open; only the one where it is open. A display duplicating the main one has no
bar of its own.
---
